{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_m3wp7dmlyts7cbvkgkk4sdwam2m7jv3oem5znmda3h3ho2gqijvq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_011vsvsE2crYxkRnZrZ9HAbV","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-oNgdf3/translation/CONFIGS.md","content":"# CONFIGS.md — Configuration-surface table (valid inputs)\n\nAxes the C code actually branches on, derived from `c_src/src/lib.c`:\n\n**A. Runtime options / modes**\n* `complexmode`'s `mode` argument — a `switch` with `case 1..4` + `default`\n  (line 115). This is the only \"mode\" selector in the library.\n* `permissions` bitmask. Inside `complexmode` it is hard-wired to `0644`, but\n  the low-level entry points `check_permissions(perms, required)` and\n  `safe_add(a, b, perms)` take it from the caller, so the whole permission\n  lattice is reachable from outside: `READ_PERM 0400`, `WRITE_PERM 0200`,\n  `EXEC_PERM 0100`, and the derived masks `0600` (`safe_add`'s requirement) and\n  `0100` (mode 4's test).\n\n**B. Input shapes**\n* integer operand magnitude/sign: zero, small positive, small negative, values\n  that make `a+b` / `a*b` overflow `int`, `INT_MIN`, `INT_MAX`.\n* `copy_and_sum` element count: `0`, `1`, `3` (what `complexmode` mode 3 uses),\n  many, negative; plus the pointer being non-NULL vs NULL.\n* string shape for `create_result_string` / `compare_operations`: empty, short,\n  long enough to make `snprintf` truncate at 64 bytes, embedded `%`\n  format-specifier characters, high bytes ≥ 0x80, and the equal / less /\n  greater orderings for `strcmp`.\n\n**C. Entry points** — all seven exported symbols, low-level first. The tests\ncall `check_permissions`, `safe_add`, `create_result_string`,\n`multiply_with_log`, `copy_and_sum`, `compare_operations` **directly** through\nthe `.so`, not only through the `complexmode` convenience wrapper.\n\nThere are no `#ifdef` compile-time branches and no cargo features, so there is a\nsingle build configuration.\n\nEvery row is driven with many randomized inputs from a fixed-seed xorshift PRNG\n(seed `0x2024_0C0D_E5EE_D001`), plus the hand-picked boundary values listed, and\nboth the return value **and** the captured `stdout` bytes are compared.\n\n| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [ ] |\n|---|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|\n| 1 | `check_permissions` | `required == 0` (vacuously satisfied for every `perms`, including `perms == 0` and negative `perms`) | [ ] |\n| 2 | `check_permissions` | single-bit `required` ∈ {`0400`,`0200`,`0100`} × `perms` covering set/clear of that bit | [ ] |\n| 3 | `check_permissions` | multi-bit `required` (`0600`, `0644`, `0777`) × `perms` with all / some / none of the bits set | [ ] |\n| 4 | `check_permissions` | full random 32-bit `perms` × `required`, incl. negative values and `INT_MIN`/`INT_MAX` as raw bit patterns | [ ] |\n| 5 | `safe_add` | `perms` grants `0600` (e.g. `0600`,`0644`,`0777`,`-1`) → returns `a+b`, random `a`,`b` | [ ] |\n| 6 | `safe_add` | `perms` grants `0600` × operands that overflow `int` (`INT_MAX`+1, `INT_MIN`-1, `INT_MAX`+`INT_MAX`) | [ ] |\n| 7 | `safe_add` | `perms` missing `0400` only, missing `0200` only, missing both → prints rejection, returns `0` | [ ] |\n| 8 | `create_result_string` | short ASCII `op` × random `val` (positive, negative, `0`, `INT_MIN`, `INT_MAX`) — compare the 64-byte returned buffer contents | [ ] |\n| 9 | `create_result_string` | empty `op` (`\"\"`) | [ ] |\n| 10 | `create_result_string` | `op` long enough that `snprintf` truncates at the 64-byte limit (boundary: `op` lengths that land the NUL exactly at 62/63/64 and beyond) | [ ] |\n| 11 | `create_result_string` | `op` containing `%d`/`%s`/`%%` (passed as data, not format) and bytes ≥ 0x80 | [ ] |\n| 12 | `multiply_with_log` | random `a`,`b` → check return value **and** the out-parameter string bytes | [ ] |\n| 13 | `multiply_with_log` | operands whose product overflows `int` (`INT_MAX*2`, `INT_MIN*-1`, `65536*65536`) and products that are `0` or negative | [ ] |\n| 14 | `copy_and_sum` | `count == 0` with a valid pointer | [ ] |\n| 15 | `copy_and_sum` | `count == 1` | [ ] |\n| 16 | `copy_and_sum` | `count == 3` (the shape `complexmode` mode 3 uses) with random values | [ ] |\n| 17 | `copy_and_sum` | `count` large (16, 64, 1024) with random values, incl. values whose running sum overflows `int` | [ ] |\n| 18 | `copy_and_sum` | all elements `INT_MAX` / all `INT_MIN` (guaranteed accumulator wraparound) | [ ] |\n| 19 | `compare_operations` | equal strings (identical bytes, incl. both empty) → `0` | [ ] |\n| 20 | `compare_operations` | unequal strings differing at the first byte / a middle byte / by length (prefix), both orderings — raw `strcmp` value must match | [ ] |\n| 21 | `compare_operations` | strings differing only in a byte ≥ 0x80 (glibc `strcmp` compares as `unsigned char`) | [ ] |\n| 22 | `compare_operations` | random byte strings of random lengths from the fixed-seed PRNG | [ ] |\n| 23 | `complexmode` | `mode == 1` (addition), random `value1`,`value2`; `value3` ignored | [ ] |\n| 24 | `complexmode` | `mode == 1` with `value1+value2` overflowing `int` | [ ] |\n| 25 | `complexmode` | `mode == 2` (multiplication + log), random `value1`,`value2` — the printed `Mode 2: Operation: multiply, Value: N` line is part of the diff | [ ] |\n| 26 | `complexmode` | `mode == 2` with `value1*value2` overflowing `int`, and with a product of `0` / negative (changes the printed digit string) | [ ] |\n| 27 | `complexmode` | `mode == 3` (array sum of all three values), random values | [ ] |\n| 28 | `complexmode` | `mode == 3` with a sum that overflows `int` | [ ] |\n| 29 | `complexmode` | `mode == 4` (complex): `permissions=0644` lacks `0100`, so the `else` branch `v1+v2+v3` is taken — random values | [ ] |\n| 30 | `complexmode` | `mode == 4` with values that overflow in the `else` branch | [ ] |\n| 31 